  1070	### 10.2 Control-center capabilities
  1071	
  1072	The user can:
  1073	
  1074	- start a workflow from a template;
  1075	- choose providers/models/effort/permissions per role before start;
  1076	- see the DAG/lane board and current loop position;
  1077	- inspect each agent’s conversation, tools, plan, task list, output, worktree, and usage;
  1078	- see parent/child relationships and provenance;
  1079	- open the agent conversation or worktree in the existing center/editor;
  1080	- pause/resume/cancel a workflow;
  1081	- cancel/retry/skip an eligible node;
  1082	- steer an active ACP agent when supported;
  1083	- answer structured input or permissions;
  1084	- approve a gate;
  1085	- compare reviewer findings;
  1086	- open artifacts, commits, PRs, test logs, and native evidence;
  1087	- save a run as a reusable workflow template.
  1088	
  1089	### 10.3 Loop visibility
  1090	
  1091	Every run exposes a deterministic loop phase:
  1092	
  1093	```ts
  1094	export type WorkflowLoopPhase =
  1095	  | 'planning'
  1096	  | 'dispatching'
  1097	  | 'implementing'
  1098	  | 'testing'
  1099	  | 'reviewing'
  1100	  | 'checking-spec'
  1101	  | 'fixing'
  1102	  | 'awaiting-human'
  1103	  | 'certifying'
  1104	  | 'complete';
  1105	```
  1106	
  1107	The phase is derived from node states/types, never guessed from assistant prose. The UI may show an agent-generated summary beside it, clearly marked as generated.
  1108	
  1109	### 10.4 Session-list behavior for workflow agents
  1110	
  1111	Workflow children do not flood the main left rail by default.
  1112	
  1113	- top-level user sessions and pinned workflow agents may appear in Working;
  1114	- all workflow agents appear in the active workflow’s tree;
  1115	- a child can be pinned to Working explicitly;
  1116	- completed workflow children remain available through the Workflow run and Session Library;
  1117	- removing a workflow run record does not silently delete provider transcripts or worktrees.
  1118	
